<title>USA: RJR sees favorable tobacco, food trends.</title>
<headline>RJR sees favorable tobacco, food trends.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>RJR Nabisco Holdings Corp said underlying trends in its tobacco business appear positive for the rest of 1997 and beyond.</p>
<p>&quot;As a rapidly growing business, we can experience volatility quarter to quarter, but the underlying trends remain very favorable for 1997 and beyond,&quot; said chairman Steven Goldstone in a news release.</p>
<p>He noted strong performance in March and indications of a stronger second quarter.</p>
<p>Goldstone also said results from the company's 80.5-percent owned Nabisco Holdings Corp food subsidiary are expected to be solid in 1997 and on track with expectations.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk, 212/859-1700))</p>
